Purpose:
The typewriter is a text editor that allows users to edit text files
on the command line. It supports typing of ASCII characters, 
backspace and enter, as well asundo and redoing of characters and 
new lines. The command menu allows users to save, exit, undo or 
redo. Files can be new or existing.

Acknowledgments:
The class chatbot.
I asked Ariel Jacobs to help test my program for bugs.

File List: 
 ActionStack.h
    ActionStacks store actions for undoing and redoing.

 ActionStack.cpp
    ActionStacks can be added to, popped from, and cleared.
    An action consists of a character, whether it was deleted,
    and its line and column.

 Editor.h
    Editor class

 Editor.cpp

 main.cpp
    Takes in the names of text file and optionally the logfile.
    If these parameters are correct, opens and runs the text editor.

 test logs:
    enter_delete: 
        a keylogger test that includes enter and then delete
    enter_delete_M.text: 
        result of running enter_delete on my typewriter
    enter_delete_T.text: 
        result of running enter_delete on the example typewriter.

    newline_undo_redo
        a keylogger test that includes making, undoing, and redoing 
        a new line.
    newline_undo_redo_M.text
        result of running newline_undo_redo on my typewriter.
    newline_undo_redo_T.text
        result of running newline_undo_redo on the example typewriter.

    type_one_line
        a keylogger test that involves writing one line.
    type_one_line_M.text
        result or running type_one_line on my typewriter.
    type_one_line_T.text
        result of running type_one_line on the example typewriter.

    undo_redo 
        a keylogger test that undoes and redoes a character.
    undo_redo_M.text
        result of running undo_redo on my typewriter.
    undo_redo_T.text
        result of running undo_redo on the example typewriter.

 Instructions:
    compile: make
    run: ./typewriter textfile.txt logfile.txt

